WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.037
Few-shot prompting adds a small number of examples before the new request.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:12.787
The examples can clarify ambiguous labels, tone, or formatting and improve consistency.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:19.237
They also consume context tokens, so include them because they improve measured performance,

00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:22.537
not simply because more examples seem better.

00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:25.722
A good example teaches the pattern you want.

00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:31.176
A poor or inconsistent example can teach the wrong pattern just as effectively.
